EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Greece_XeniasTheLeperOfHouseTytalus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Xenias the Leper of House Tytalus"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Xenias the Leper of House Tytalus (Chapter Five: Greece, p63): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t1cc4ca8aa42d1b1abd026a ^"Xenias the Leper of House Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t88f9980f616d446ddb5dd2 ^"Epidauros"]
            ^"Age" STRING "165 (Apparent Age: 107)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Dutiful +3, Calm +3, Driven +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 63
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Xenias, the nominal leader of the covenant by simple virtue of being the eldest, is a magus aegrotus (a leper magus; see *Houses of Hermes: Societates*, page 95). Like all the leper Tytalus magi, he has a great affinity for healing and longevity, and is probably the Tribunal’s foremost expert in such matters. He appears to be a disheveled old man dressed in slightly tattered leper’s robes. The linen veil drawn across his face and his elbow-length gloves disguise just how ancient and withered he really is, and a constantly clanking bell tied to his robes warns people of his status as a leper. Although Twilight-ridden, Xenias is approachable enough, not that many magi do — the prejudices against lepers are not restricted only to mundanes, especially since magic cannot cure leprosy."
    }

}
